¶
'''bacchantic''' (ba-kan′tik), ''a.'' [< ''bacchant'' + ''-ic.''] Of or resembling a bacchant or bacchanal; bacchanalian; riotous; jovial.
{{smaller block|It is the feeblest band [of music]; and yet it is subject to spurts of ''bacchantic'' fervor.
{{right|''C. D. Warner'', Winter on the Nile, p. 103.}}
I hardly know what of ''bacchantic'' joyousness I had not attributed to them [the Italians] on their holidays.
{{right|''Howells'', Venetian Life, xviii.}}}}

